hadiths[36]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1830","[AI-translation] The hadith of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: Allah has opened of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this, and he gestured with his hand indicating ninety.""
1831"""
"1831","Narrated 'Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""An army will invade the Ka'bah, and when they reach al-Baida' (a place in the desert), those in the front and those in the rear of them will be swallowed up (by the earth)."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, how will those in the front and those in the rear of them be swallowed up when among them are their marketers and those who do not belong to them (i.e., not part of the army)?"" He said: ""Those in the front and those in the rear of them will be swallowed up, then they will be resurrected according to their intentions."""
"1832","Narrated Usama:\n\nOnce the Prophet (ﷺ) stood at the top of a (looked out from upon one) castle amongst the castles (or the \nhigh buildings) of Medina and said, \Do you see what I see? (No doubt) I see the spots where \nafflictions will take place among your houses (and these afflictions will be) as numerous as the spots \nwhere raindrops fall.\"""""""""
"1833","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There will be afflictions (in the near future) during which a sitting person will be better than a standing one"""
"1834","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping ""1835"",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents ""1836"",Narrated Hudhaifa:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) once delivered a speech in front of us wherein he left nothing but mentioned (about) \neverything that would happen till the Hour. Some of us stored that our minds and some forgot it. \n(After that speech) I used to see events taking place (which had been referred to in that speech) but I \nhad forgotten them (before their occurrence). Then I would recognize such events as a man recognizes \nanother man who has been absent and then sees and recognizes him."""
"1835","[AI-translation] The hadith of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: The Hour will not be established until two groups fight, and there will be a great massacre between them, while their call is one.""
1836"""
"1836","Narrated Hudhaifah (رضي الله عنه): The Prophet (ﷺ) once delivered a sermon to us in which he left nothing untold, from that time up to the establishment of the Hour, but mentioned it - those who retained it in memory retained it, and those who forgot it forgot it. Sometimes I would see something which I had forgotten, then I would recognize it just as a man recognizes another man who had been absent from him, and when he sees him again, he recognizes him."
"1837","Narrated Hudhaifah: We were sitting with 'Umar (رضي الله عنه) when he said, ""Which of you remembers the statement of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about the Fitnah?"" I said, ""I do, exactly as he said it."" He said, ""You are indeed daring concerning it."" I said, ""The Fitnah of a man in his family, his wealth, his children, and his neighbor is atoned for by prayer, fasting, charity, and enjoining good and forbidding evil."" He said, ""This is not what I want, but rather the Fitnah which will surge like the surging of the sea."" I said, ""There is no harm for you regarding it, O Commander of the Believers, for there is a closed door between you and it."" He asked, ""Will the door be broken or opened?"" I said, ""It will be broken."" He said, ""Then it will never be closed again."" We asked, ""Did 'Umar know what the door was?"" He said, ""Yes, just as he knew that there is a night before tomorrow. I narrated to him a hadith that was free from errors."" We were afraid to ask Hudhaifah, so we ordered Masruq to ask him, and he said, ""The door was 'Umar."""
"1838","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Soon the river ""Euphrates"" will disclose the treasure (the mountain) of gold"""
"1839","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There are angels coming to you in succession at night"""
"1840","That he heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying in the year of the Conquest (of Mecca) while he was in Mecca, Allah and His Apostle have made the selling of wine (i.e. alcoholic drinks) unlawful."""""""""
"1841","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""The Hour will not be established till a man from Qahtan appears, driving the people with his stick."""""""
"1842","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"""
"1843","Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"""
"1844","Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78) ""1845"",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""
"1845","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: The Hour will not be established until you fight a people whose shoes are of hair, and the Hour will not be established until you fight a people whose faces are like hammered shields.""
1846"""
"1846","Narrated Abu Huraira (رضي الله عنه): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""This tribe of Quraish will bring destruction to the people."" They said, ""What do you order us to do?"" He said, ""Would that the people kept away from them."""
"1847","Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"""
"1848","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""When Khosrau is ruined, there will be no Khosrau after him; and when Caesar is ruined, their will be no Caesar after him. By Him in Whose Hands my life is, you will spend their treasures in Allah's Cause."""""""
"1849","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping ""1850"",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""
"1850","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: The Hour will not be established until nearly thirty Dajjals, liars, are sent, each of them claiming that he is the Messenger of Allah.""
1851"""
"1851","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: 'Umar went with a group of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), along with the Prophet (ﷺ), to Ibn Sayyad, until they found him playing with the boys near the fort of Bani Maghalah. Ibn Sayyad had, at that time, almost reached the age of puberty. He did not notice (their presence) until the Prophet (ﷺ) struck him on the back with his hand. The Prophet (ﷺ) then said, ""Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" Ibn Sayyad looked at him and said, ""I testify that you are the Messenger of the unlettered people."" Then Ibn Sayyad asked the Prophet (ﷺ), ""Do you testify that I am the messenger of Allah?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""I believe in Allah and His Messengers."" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""What do you see?"" Ibn Sayyad said, ""A true one and a false one come to me."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""The matter has been confused for you."" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""I have kept something hidden for you."" Ibn Sayyad said, ""It is Ad-Dukh."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Away with you! You cannot go beyond your limit."" 'Umar said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to strike his neck."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""If he is he (i.e. the Dajjal), you will not be able to overpower him, and if he is not he, then there is no good for you in killing him."""
"1852","Narrated Ibn Umar:\n\n (Later on) Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (once again) went along with Ubai bin Ka'b \n to the garden of date-palms where Ibn Saiyad was staying. When the \n Prophet entered the garden, he started hiding himself behind the \n trunks of the date-palms as he wanted to hear something from the Ibn \n Saiyad before the latter could see him. Ibn Saiyad was lying in his \n bed, covered with a velvet sheet from where his murmurs were heard. \n Ibn Saiyad's mother saw the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was hiding himself behind\n the trunks of the date-palms. She addressed Ibn Saiyad, \O Saf!\"" (And \n this was his name). Ibn Saiyad got up. The Prophet (ﷺ) said"""
"1853","(Later on) Messenger of Allah ﷺ (once again) went along with Ubai bin Ka'b to the garden of date-palms where Ibn Saiyad was staying. When the Prophet entered the garden, he started hiding himself behind the trunks of the date-palms as he wanted to hear something from the Ibn Saiyad before the latter could see him. Ibn Saiyad was lying in his bed, covered with a velvet sheet from where his murmurs were heard. Ibn Saiyad's mother saw the Prophet ﷺ while he was hiding himself behind the trunks of the date-palms. She addressed Ibn Saiyad, ""O Saf!"" (And this was his name). Ibn Saiyad got up. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Had this woman let him to himself, he would have revealed the reality of his case."" Then the Prophet ﷺ got up amongst the people, glorifying Allah as He deserves, he mentioned Ad-Dajjal, saying, ""I warn you about him (i.e. Ad-Dajjal) and there is no prophet who did not warn his nation about him, and Noah warned his nation about him, but I tell you a statement which no prophet informed his nation of. You should understand that he is a one-eyed man and Allah is not one-eyed."""" ""1854"",This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Anas through another chain of transmitters"""
"1854","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) mentioned Al-Masih Ad-Dajjal one day among the people, and said: Allah is not one-eyed. Behold, Al-Masih Ad-Dajjal is blind in the right eye, as if his eye is a floating grape.""
1855"""
"1855","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""No prophet was sent but that he warned his nation against the one-eyed liar (i.e., the Dajjal). Beware, he is one-eyed, and verily your Lord is not one-eyed, and between his (the Dajjal's) eyes is written 'Kafir' (disbeliever)."""
"1856","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Abu 'Awanah narrated to us; 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, who said: 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr said to Hudhayfah: ""Will you not narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?"" He said: ""I heard him say: 'Indeed, with the Dajjal when he emerges will be water and fire. As for that which people see as fire, it is cold water; and as for that which people see as cold water, it is fire that burns. So whoever among you encounters him, let him fall into that which he sees as fire, for it is sweet, cold water.'"" Hudhayfah said: ""And I heard him say: 'A man from those who were before you was approached by the angel to take his soul. It was said to him: ""Did you do any good?"" He said: ""I do not know."" It was said: ""Look."" He said: ""I do not know anything except that I used to conduct business with people in the world and give them respite; I would grant respite to the wealthy and pardon the destitute."" So Allah admitted him into Paradise.'"" He said: ""And I heard him say: 'A man was attended by death. When he despaired of life, he instructed his family: ""When I die, gather much firewood for me and kindle a fire therein until it consumes my flesh and reaches my bone and I am pulverized. Then take it, grind it, then look for a windy day and scatter it in the sea."" They did so. Allah gathered him and said: ""Why did you do that?"" He said: ""From fear of You."" So Allah forgave him.'"" 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr said: ""And I heard him narrate that, and he was a grave-digger."""""""
"1857","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Shall I not tell you about the Dajjal a story of which no prophet told his nation? The Dajjall is one-eyed and will bring with him what will resemble Hell and Paradise"""
"1858","One day Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) narrated to us a long narration about Ad-Dajjal and among the things he narrated to us, was: Ad-Dajjal will come ""1859"",Mughira b. Shu'ba reported:No one asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) more about Dajjil than I asked him. He said: He should not be a source of worry to you for he would not be able to do any harm to you. I said: Allah's Messenger"""
"1859","[AI-translation] Mughira bin Shuba, he said: No one asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about Ad-Dajjal as much as I asked him. He said to me: What harms you concerning him? I said: Because they say that with him is a mountain of bread and a river of water. He said: He is of less concern to Allah than that.""
1860"""
"1860","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""There is no land but the Dajjal will tread upon it, except Makkah and Madinah, for there is not a single one of their passes but has angels guarding it, standing in ranks. Then Madinah will shake with its inhabitants three times, and Allah will expel from it every disbeliever and hypocrite."""
"1861","heard Allah's Messengpu rrb.- saying: (It will be) from among t most wicked people whof will be livin at the time when the Hou will SZ. fne noof oterz established"""" ""1862"",Ibn `Umar reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:The pious dreams are the seventieth part of Prophecy ""1863"",It is narrated on the authority of ('Abdullah) son of Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (may peace of Allah be upon him) said:(The superstructure of) al-Islam is raised on five (pillars)"""
"1862","[AI-translation] Narrated Sahl bin Sad (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) pointing with his two fingers like this, with the middle and the one next to the thumb, saying: I was sent and the Hour are like these two.""
1863"""
"1863","Narrated Anas: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""I have been sent, and the Hour (i.e., the Day of Judgment) is like these two,"" and he joined his index and middle fingers together."
"1864","Narrated Abu Huraira (RA): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Between the two blowing (of the Trumpet) there will be forty."" Someone asked, ""Forty days?"" He (Abu Huraira) said, ""I refused (to say anything)."" They asked, ""Forty months?"" He said, ""I refused (to say anything)."" They asked, ""Forty years?"" He said, ""I refused (to say anything)."" Then (the Prophet said), ""Then Allah will send down rain from the sky, and they (the dead) will spring up (from their graves) just as vegetables sprout. There is nothing of the human body that does not decay except one bone, which is the coccyx (the small bone at the base of the spine), and from it the whole body will be reconstructed on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1865","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, When carried to his grave"""
